skill: "ambassador-event-ops"
sections[3]:
  - "# ambassador-event-ops\n\nOperate the ambassador program and the event runbook: tiers and criteria, contribution tracking, event logistics with consent and code-of-conduct handling, and the post-event report. Use when onboarding or reviewing ambassadors, when an event is planned, and within 72 hours after every event while evidence is fresh.\n\nOwner: role-community-manager (pod-customer, marketing). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"ambassador policy ambassador-policy.toon (tiers, criteria, perks); contribution records; event plan; event policy event-policy.toon (consent, conduct, moderation staffing)\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/community/ambassador-register.toon with tier, activity and perks issued; event-runbook.toon; post-event-report.toon with metrics\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Load ambassador-policy.toon; record tier criteria and perks issued so recognition is arithmetic on policy, not favor.\n2. Review ambassador activity monthly against criteria; promotions and demotions list the criterion rows that moved, and borderline cases wait one more period instead of being forced.\n3. Instantiate event-runbook.toon from event-policy.toon for each event: venue or platform, consent notices, code-of-conduct point person, moderation shift schedule and escalation contacts.\n4. Confirm consent and recording rules before the event: what is recorded, where it is published and how a participant withdraws consent mid-event.\n5. Run the moderation shift as scheduled; moderation during events follows moderation-escalation-ladder, and event-specific rules sit inside that ladder, not beside it.\n6. Within 72 hours, assemble the post-event report: attendance, new-member conversion, content produced, incidents and their handling.\n7. Log ambassador contributions evidenced by the event (talks, help threads, content) into the register with links.\n8. Emit ask_question for budget exceptions and for any conduct case above warn level; archive the runbook with the report so the next event starts from precedent.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nconduct cases to moderation-escalation-ladder; metrics brief to community and growth leads.\n"
